{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-009", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "New Zealand to give duty-free access to Bangladesh post LDC graduation", "content": "New Zealand is keen on continuing duty-free and preferential market access facilities for Bangladesh even after the country’s LDC graduation, the former’s non-resident high commissioner to the latter David Pine said. \nBoth sides discussed ways to further expand bilateral trade and investment ties, make use of existing regional trade frameworks and the possibility of signing a comprehensive bilateral FTA. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/new-zealand-to-give-duty-free-access-to-bangladesh-post-ldc-graduation-310383-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-010", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "India-EU FTA to be implemented by 2026 end: European Commission prez", "content": "European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen recently vowed to implement the India-EU FTA by 2026 end, announcing to make the deal ‘fully operational at record speed’. \nThe moment will be marked by a business event for European and Indian firms, she said in Gothenburg. \nIndian PM Modi invited European industry leaders to partner with India in digital infrastructure, AI and clean energy. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-eu-fta-to-be-implemented-by-2026-end-european-commission-prez-310380-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-011", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["concerns"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India reimposes polyester yarn QCO after Gujarat HC stay", "content": "India has reimposed Quality Control Order (QCO) compliance on polyester yarn imports after the Gujarat High Court stayed the withdrawal of QCOs for FDY, POY and DTY.\nThe move is expected to support domestic producers through tighter import checks, while increasing compliance costs and creating supply concerns for downstream textile industries dependent on imported yarn.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-reimposes-polyester-yarn-qco-after-gujarat-hc-stay-310379-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-012", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India, Netherlands to raise bilateral trade, market access, investment", "content": "India and the Netherlands have agreed to raise bilateral trade, market access and investment, especially in high-potential sectors like textiles, renewable energy, infrastructure and organic chemicals. \nThis will be done through joint ventures, industrial partnerships and tech collaboration between companies from both sides. \nBoth agreed to elevate their bilateral relationship to a strategic partnership. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-netherlands-to-raise-bilateral-trade-market-access-investment-310378-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-013", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Polyester yarn prices rise in India on firmer feedstock costs", "content": "Polyester yarn prices in India moved higher, supported by stronger PTA, MEG and melt costs that prompted producers to raise POY, DTY, PTY and FDY prices.\nDespite soft and volatile crude oil trends, higher feedstock costs, tighter availability in some segments and import pressures supported the uptrend, with sentiment expected to remain firm if raw material costs stay elevated.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/polyester-yarn-prices-rise-in-india-on-firmer-feedstock-costs-310376-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-014", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["leading"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Vietnam’s FDI sector contributes over 20% of GDP: Deputy PM", "content": "Vietnam’s FDI sector contributes more than a fifth of the GDP, accounting for around seven-tenths of the export turnover, Deputy PM Nguyen Van Thang said. \nAmid falling global FDI flows into several regions, Vietnam continues as a leading FDI destination in ASEAN, he said. \nNguyen said Vietnam will continue promoting institutional reforms and improving the investment and business environment. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-s-fdi-sector-contributes-over-20-of-gdp-deputy-pm-310370-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-015", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["concerns", "weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Inflation cuts deep into consumer spending in Bangladesh: DCCI index", "content": "High inflation is cutting deep into Bangladesh consumer spending, with weak demand turning one of the biggest concerns for businesses, DCCI said. \nHigher rents, utility bills and fuel prices are eating away at already thin profit margins. \nDCCI’s economic position index revealed that consumers have sharply reduced spending as the cost of living continues to rise. \nSMEs are feeling the pressure the most. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/inflation-cuts-deep-into-consumer-spending-in-bangladesh-dcci-index-310369-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-016", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "EU green mandates and the Vietnam T&A industry", "content": "Vietnam’s textile and footwear exporters are accelerating sustainability efforts as stricter EU regulations reshape market access requirements. \nRising compliance pressure from measures such as CBAM and ESPR is pushing manufacturers toward circular production, cleaner technologies and greater supply-chain transparency, though limited green finance remains a major challenge for smaller firms. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/eu-green-mandates-and-the-vietnam-t-a-industry-310361-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-017", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "US’ Aramark’s Q2 revenue grows on US, international gains", "content": "Aramark has reported revenue of $4.9 billion in Q2 FY26, up 15 per cent YoY, driven by new business wins and growth across US and international operations. \nOperating income rose 26 per cent to $220 million, while adjusted EPS grew 40 per cent. \nCash flow strengthened, client retention exceeded 98 per cent, and the company raised its organic revenue outlook. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-aramark-s-q2-revenue-grows-on-us-international-gains-310386-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-018", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "improve", "[否定]weak", "[否定]uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "South Korea’s Misto Holdings Q1 revenue rises 4.2% to $867.3 mn", "content": "Misto Holdings has reported a strong Q1 2026, with consolidated revenue rising 4.2 per cent YoY to KRW 1.3 trillion (~$867.3 million) and operating profit increasing 19 per cent to KRW 193.7 billion. \nGrowth was driven by Acushnet, improved Misto profitability, China expansion, K-fashion momentum, and Fila product gains, despite macroeconomic uncertainty, tariffs and weak consumer sentiment. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/south-korea-s-misto-holdings-q1-revenue-rises-4-2-to-867-3-mn-310381-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
